@rocketandsquash here. This egg’s an absolute cracker — right up there among my favourites in Good Eggs. The lacy and crisp cheese skirt make a ridiculously moreish base. Which is great on its own, on toast or in a sandwich with some Worcestershire sauce and a chilli oil ... but maybe best of all as I had it when I visited the Mob studio: held within a warmed corn tortilla, and loaded with a fresh salsa made from finely diced jalapeno, shallots, a little coriander and a load of lime. The finer details are on Mob’s website. Check it out, make the egg this weekend[, then grab a copy of my book ;) ].

